  "title": "Albanese government considers 'world-leading' ban on smart glasses in public offices and buildings",
  "summary": "Minister for public service states the ban poses 'legitimate privacy and security concerns' in Commonwealth-run workplaces, while councils push the technology out of public spaces over privacy fears.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Albanese government is considering a 'world-leading' ban on smart glasses in public offices and service centres.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The government has avoided a sweeping ban on the import of the camera-equipped technology and encouraged individual workplaces to set their own rules.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The ban aims to address privacy and security concerns in Commonwealth-run workplaces.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
