      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/18/labor-migration-plan-tony-burke-coalition-qantas-renewable-energy-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow the day’s news live</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia needs to slow down its artificial intelligence use and create better security laws, the companies creating the technology have told the federal government.</p><p>In a submission to an ongoing inquiry, <strong>OpenAI</strong> said national leaders had a responsibility to work with other countries to stop global security threats:</p><p>Many of the most consequential risks will not stop at national borders, making international co-ordination increasingly important.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/18/labor-migration-plan-tony-burke-coalition-qantas-renewable-energy-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
